## Loop

```
1  user opens coordinator (opus) session
2  coordinator reads project.state + git log + builder patchlogs
3  coordinator updates state · refines next builder prompt (lives inside slice codon)
4  user copies builder prompt → opens IDE session (sonnet ok) → pastes
5  builder executes one slice · commits · appends one PATCHLOG line to slice + state codons
6  next coordinator session: back to step 2
```

User is in the loop only at session boundaries and judgment calls.
Coordinator owns sequence and prompts. Builder owns code.

